---
/**
 * Blueprint, the starhold.fyi hero motif. STAR-166 round 2 (Opus drawing, wired
 * by F1): an exploded assembly drawing of the station's core module on a
 * drawing sheet. Three parts stacked on one chain-line axis (cap plate with
 * mast and dish, the hab ring, the docking collar), a projected side elevation
 * on the right, numbered callouts and one dimension.
 *
 * Two layers: .far is the construction geometry (assembly axis, projection
 * lines, hidden edges dashed as on a real drawing), thin and dim; the parts
 * are at full weight, and the hab ring's outline carries a 3-unit stroke
 * attribute so the nearest silhouette is heaviest. Colour is never a literal:
 * every stroke and fill is currentColor, and the fleet-base .fleet-art classes
 * point it at tokens. The faint technical grid behind it is the hero's grid
 * paper (fyi.css, F3). preserveAspectRatio="xMinYMid slice" lets the hero crop
 * the sheet at the viewport edge (F1). Motion is CSS only and finite.
 * Decorative, so hidden from assistive tech; the SVG text is drawing
 * annotation, not content.
 */
---

<svg class="fleet-art fyi-art" viewBox="0 0 480 480" preserveAspectRatio="xMinYMid slice" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
	<!-- sheet: frame, edge ticks, title block -->
	<g class="lane">
		<rect x="8" y="8" width="464" height="464" rx="2"/>
